[[File:Mister Elegance (Beta 46.0).png|thumb|257x257px|Beta 46.0]]
Mister (Mr.) Elegance reversed its effect in the first major update after release. For as when in '''Beta 30.0''' it would deal 4 DMG to enemy monsters summoned in front of it (making it similar to [[Astigmatism]]), '''Beta 31.0''' will now let it deal 2 DMG to enemy monsters NOT summoned in front of it (making it more similar to [[Heats Flamesman]]).
[[File:Mister Elegance (Beta 49.0).png|thumb|Beta 49.0]]
'''Beta 35.0''' completely reworked it. Dropping its cost from 8G to 5G with stats from 4/6 to 2/5 (-3G -2/-1 total), its new effect includes Taunt and a special Turn Start and End effect. When your turn ends, it gains +2 ATK and when it starts, it gains -2 ATK. This effectively means that it has 2 extra ATK during the enemy's turn, making it a 4/5 Taunt for 5G. '''Beta 36.1''' droped its cost to 4G, making it equal to [[Mister Society|Mr. Society]]'s. '''Beta 41.0''' reworked the card engine, which allowed 'aura' effects to work. This resulted in this card getting reworked to passively gain +2 ATK during the opponent's turn.

'''Beta 46.0''' added [[Chessboard]] and the [[:Category:Piece|Piece]] Tribe with 5 members, this being one of them. As a result, it was entirely reworked again. In stats, it gained +1/+1/-1, leaving it at 3/4 back at 5G. In effect, like the others, it uses the same "played left or right" type of effect already used by Mr. Society. In this case, it gains +1 ATK, Taunt AND +1 Thorns when played on the left. When played on the right, it gains +1 Armor instead. '''Beta 49.0''' made its left effect give it +1 HP instead of +1 Thorns (as Thorns was removed as a whole), thus it now gains +1/+1 and Taunt. During the next big Piece change of '''Beta 54.0''', this was buffed by giving it both effects if you have a [[Chessboard]] on the board.
